public with sharing class RecordAccessService {

    /**
     * Returns the subset of recordIds that the running user can edit,
     * as determined by the UserRecordAccess object (HasEditAccess = true).
     *
     * @param recordIds  Up to 2,000 record IDs (may span multiple objects).
     *                   Null or empty input yields an empty set (never null).
     * @return           Set of IDs for which the current user has edit access.
     */
    public static Set<Id> editableIds(Set<Id> recordIds) {
        Set<Id> editableSet = new Set<Id>();

        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {
            return editableSet;
        }

        // Convert to a list for chunked subList access
        List<Id> idList = new List<Id>(recordIds);

        // SOQL IN-clause limit is 1,000 values; 2,000 IDs → at most 2 queries
        Integer chunkSize = 1000;

        for (Integer i = 0; i < idList.size(); i += chunkSize) {
            Integer end = Math.min(i + chunkSize, idList.size());
            List<Id> chunk = idList.subList(i, end);

            for (UserRecordAccess ura : [
                SELECT SobjectRowId
                FROM UserRecordAccess
                WHERE SobjectRowId IN :chunk
                AND HasEditAccess = true
            ]) {
                editableSet.add(ura.SobjectRowId);
            }
        }

        return editableSet;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Null / empty input** | Early return of a new (non-null) `Set<Id>()`. |
| **Mixed object types** | `SobjectRowId` is the globally-unique 18-character record ID, so a single `UserRecordAccess` query covers all objects without needing to know or group by `SObjectType`. |
| **SOQL governor limit (20 queries)** | The IN-clause is capped at 1,000 values (SOQL limit). 2,000 IDs → **2 SOQL queries**, well under the 20-query budget. |
| **Multiple access paths** | A user may have several `UserRecordAccess` rows for the same record (ownership, role, explicit share, Modify All, etc.). Filtering on `HasEditAccess = true` and collecting into a `Set` naturally deduplicates. |
| **`with sharing`** | Applied at class level per the spec. `UserRecordAccess` is a system "access-report" object inherently scoped to the current user, so the modifier is belt-and-suspenders but correct per convention. |
| **Bulk-safe** | No per-record DML, no nested loops over records; the only loop is over the small number of chunks (≤ 2) and the result rows. |

